IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART III -- regulations 17 to 21: EMPLOYMENT IN
-- INTERNATIONAL TRANSPORTATION (ships, aircraft, trains, motor vehicles). Piece cr1. LAYER 1.
--
-- Regulation 17 sets the frame (employment in international transportation is excepted unless a later regulation
-- includes it, and the inclusions of 18 to 21 stand only if the employment would be pensionable if wholly within
-- Canada); regulations 18 to 21 each include one kind of such employment. "Employment in international
-- transportation" and "employer operating in Canada" are defined in regulation 15(1) (cr1-part3-interpretation);
-- here each is a plain BOOLEAN input, to be filled from those rules.
-- A basis "approved by the Minister" (regulation 20) is the Minister's judgment: a plain input, never guessed.

§ `Regulations, Part III -- regulations 17 to 21: employment in international transportation`

§§ `Regulation 17`

-- 17 (1) Notwithstanding sections 18, 19, 20 and 21, employment in international transportation described in
-- those sections is not pensionable employment unless it is employment that would be pensionable employment if it
-- were wholly within Canada.
-- src:263 | 17 (1) Notwithstanding sections 18, 19, 20 and 21, employment in international transportation described in those sections is not pensionable employment unless it is employment that would be pensionable employment if it were wholly within Canada.
@ref Reg 17(1) (src:263)
GIVEN `the employment is described in section 18, 19, 20 or 21` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were wholly within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 17(1) — employment in international transportation described in sections 18 to 21 is pensionable employment` `the employment is described in section 18, 19, 20 or 21` `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were wholly within Canada` MEANS
    `the employment is described in section 18, 19, 20 or 21` AND `the employment would be pensionable employment if it were wholly within Canada`

-- 17 (2) Employment in international transportation, except employment therein that is included in pensionable
-- employment by section 18, 19, 20, or 22, is excepted from pensionable employment. The list names 18, 19, 20 and
-- 22 and not 21, though section 21 also includes such employment: read literally, section 21's inclusion would
-- be excepted again. The rule takes 21 as one more inclusion (fork F12).
-- src:264 | (2) Employment in international transportation, except employment therein that is included in pensionable employment by section 18, 19, 20, or 22, is excepted from pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 17(2) (src:264)
GIVEN `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 21` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 22` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 17(2) — employment in international transportation is excepted from pensionable employment` `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 18` `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 19` `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 20` `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 21` `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 22` MEANS
    NOT (    `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 18`
         OR  `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 19`
         OR  `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 20`
         OR  `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 21`
         OR  `the employment is included in pensionable employment by section 22`)

§§ `Regulation 18: ships`

-- 18 (3) For the purposes of this section, a person has a place of domicile in Canada if (a) the person is a
-- Canadian citizen; or (b) the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of the Immigration and Refugee
-- Protection Act and has a place in Canada to which they return from time to time as their place of permanent abode.
-- src:271 | (3) For the purposes of this section, a person has a place of domicile in Canada if
-- src:272 | (a) the person is a Canadian citizen; or
-- src:273 | (b) the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act and has a place in Canada to which they return from time to time as their place of permanent abode.
@ref Reg 18(3) (src:271-273)
GIVEN `the person is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a place in Canada to which they return from time to time as their place of permanent abode` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(3) — a person has a place of domicile in Canada` `the person is a Canadian citizen` `the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` `the person has a place in Canada to which they return from time to time as their place of permanent abode` MEANS
        `the person is a Canadian citizen`
    OR  (    `the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act`
         AND `the person has a place in Canada to which they return from time to time as their place of permanent abode`)

-- 18 (4) agreement with the crew means articles of agreement entered into under the Canada Shipping Act, 2001.
-- src:275 | agreement with the crew means articles of agreement entered into under the Canada Shipping Act, 2001. (contrat d’engagement de l’équipage)
@ref Reg 18(4) "agreement with the crew" (src:275)
GIVEN `the agreement is articles of agreement entered into under the Canada Shipping Act, 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(4) — an agreement is an agreement with the crew` `the agreement is articles of agreement entered into under the Canada Shipping Act, 2001` MEANS
    `the agreement is articles of agreement entered into under the Canada Shipping Act, 2001`

-- src:276 | inland voyage means a voyage on
-- src:277 | (a) any river, lake or other navigable fresh waters within Canada, including the St. Lawrence River as far seaward as a straight line drawn from Cap-des-Rosiers to West Point, Anticosti Island and from Anticosti Island to the north shore of the St. Lawrence River along a meridian of longitude 63° W.;
-- src:278 | (b) any part of any lake or river forming part of the inland waters of Canada that lies within the United States;
-- src:279 | (c) Lake Michigan; or
-- src:280 | (d) any sheltered waters on the coasts of Canada that are described in Schedule 1 to the Vessel Safety Certificates Regulations. (voyage en eaux internes)
@ref Reg 18(4) "inland voyage" (src:276-280)
DECLARE `cr1 Waters on which a voyage is made` IS ONE OF
    `any river, lake or other navigable fresh waters within Canada, including the St. Lawrence River as far seaward as a straight line drawn from Cap-des-Rosiers to West Point, Anticosti Island and from Anticosti Island to the north shore of the St. Lawrence River along a meridian of longitude 63° W.`
    `any part of any lake or river forming part of the inland waters of Canada that lies within the United States`
    `Lake Michigan`
    `any sheltered waters on the coasts of Canada that are described in Schedule 1 to the Vessel Safety Certificates Regulations`
    `other waters`

-- inland voyage means a voyage on (a) fresh waters within Canada, (b) the part of an inland water of Canada that
-- lies within the United States, (c) Lake Michigan, or (d) the sheltered waters on the coasts of Canada described
-- in Schedule 1 to the Vessel Safety Certificates Regulations (not deposited: a judgment the caller states).
@ref Reg 18(4) "inland voyage" (src:276-280)
GIVEN waters IS A `cr1 Waters on which a voyage is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(4) — a voyage is an inland voyage` waters MEANS
    CONSIDER waters
    WHEN `other waters` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 18 (1) In the case of an employer who is operating in Canada and who employs persons in international
-- transportation on a ship that is operated under an agreement with the crew that is entered into in Canada,
-- pensionable employment includes (a) when that ship is engaged on a voyage other than an inland voyage, the
-- employment on the ship of any person who has a place of domicile in Canada; and (b) when that ship is engaged
-- on an inland voyage, all persons employed on the ship.
-- src:267 | 18 (1) In the case of an employer who is operating in Canada and who employs persons in international transportation on a ship that is operated under an agreement with the crew that is entered into in Canada, pensionable employment includes
-- src:268 | (a) when that ship is engaged on a voyage other than an inland voyage, the employment on the ship of any person who has a place of domicile in Canada; and
-- src:269 | (b) when that ship is engaged on an inland voyage, all persons employed on the ship.
@ref Reg 18(1) (src:267-269)
GIVEN `the employer is an employer operating in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is operated under an agreement with the crew that is entered into in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is engaged on an inland voyage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a place of domicile in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(1) — pensionable employment includes the employment on the ship under an agreement with the crew` `the employer is an employer operating in Canada` `the ship is operated under an agreement with the crew that is entered into in Canada` `the ship is engaged on an inland voyage` `the person has a place of domicile in Canada` MEANS
        `the employer is an employer operating in Canada`
    AND `the ship is operated under an agreement with the crew that is entered into in Canada`
    AND (`the ship is engaged on an inland voyage` OR `the person has a place of domicile in Canada`)

-- 18 (2) Where an employer operating in Canada employs persons in international transportation on a ship that
-- is not operating under an agreement with the crew, pensionable employment includes all employment on the ship if
-- it is being operated mainly in and near Canada. A ship under an agreement with the crew entered into outside
-- Canada is within neither (1) nor (2) (finding in NOTES.md).
-- src:270 | (2) Where an employer operating in Canada employs persons in international transportation on a ship that is not operating under an agreement with the crew, pensionable employment includes all employment on the ship if it is being operated mainly in and near Canada.
@ref Reg 18(2) (src:270)
GIVEN `the employer is an employer operating in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is operating under an agreement with the crew` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is being operated mainly in and near Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 18(2) — pensionable employment includes the employment on the ship not under an agreement with the crew` `the employer is an employer operating in Canada` `the ship is operating under an agreement with the crew` `the ship is being operated mainly in and near Canada` MEANS
        `the employer is an employer operating in Canada`
    AND (NOT `the ship is operating under an agreement with the crew`)
    AND `the ship is being operated mainly in and near Canada`

§§ `Regulation 19: aircraft`

-- 19 Pensionable employment includes employment in international transportation on an aircraft used in the
-- operation of a commercial air service by a person who is licensed to operate an international service and a
-- domestic service under the Canada Transportation Act. (Regulation 15(1) asks only for an international service.)
-- src:283 | 19 Pensionable employment includes employment in international transportation on an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service by a person who is licensed to operate an international service and a domestic service under the Canada Transportation Act.
@ref Reg 19 (src:283)
GIVEN `the employment is in international transportation on an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate a domestic service under the Canada Transportation Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 19 — pensionable employment includes the employment on the aircraft` `the employment is in international transportation on an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service` `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act` `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate a domestic service under the Canada Transportation Act` MEANS
        `the employment is in international transportation on an aircraft used in the operation of a commercial air service`
    AND `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate an international service under the Canada Transportation Act`
    AND `the person who operates the service is licensed to operate a domestic service under the Canada Transportation Act`

§§ `Regulation 20: freight and passenger trains`

-- 20 (1) Pensionable employment includes, in the case of employment in international transportation on a freight
-- or passenger train operated by a railway company whose principal place of business is in Canada, that part of
-- the employment of a person that is determined by the employer (on a basis approved by the Minister) to be in
-- respect of employment in Canada. (3) railway company has the same meaning as in the Canada Transportation Act
-- (an input). The answer is the part the employer determined, in the unit the employer uses; NOTHING if the
-- subsection does not apply or the Minister has not approved the basis.
-- src:286 | 20 (1) Pensionable employment includes, in the case of employment in international transportation on a freight or passenger train operated by a railway company whose principal place of business is in Canada, that part of the employment of a person that is determined by the employer (on a basis approved by the Minister) to be in respect of employment in Canada.
-- src:288 | (3) In this section, railway company has the same meaning as in the Canada Transportation Act.
@ref Reg 20(1), 20(3) (src:286), (src:288)
GIVEN `the employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the train is operated by a railway company within the meaning of the Canada Transportation Act whose principal place of business is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the employment determined by the employer to be in respect of employment in Canada` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister has approved the basis on which the employer determined it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 20(1) — the part of the employment on a train of a Canadian railway company that is pensionable employment` `the employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train` `the train is operated by a railway company within the meaning of the Canada Transportation Act whose principal place of business is in Canada` `the part of the employment determined by the employer to be in respect of employment in Canada` `the Minister has approved the basis on which the employer determined it` MEANS
    IF     `the employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train`
       AND `the train is operated by a railway company within the meaning of the Canada Transportation Act whose principal place of business is in Canada`
       AND `the Minister has approved the basis on which the employer determined it`
    THEN JUST `the part of the employment determined by the employer to be in respect of employment in Canada`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 20 (2) ... on a train operated by a railway company whose principal place of business is outside Canada, that
-- part of the employment of a person who is resident in Canada that is determined by the employer (on a basis
-- approved by the Minister) to be in respect of employment in Canada.
-- src:287 | (2) Pensionable employment includes, in the case of employment in international transportation on a freight or passenger train operated by a railway company whose principal place of business is outside Canada, that part of the employment of a person who is resident in Canada that is determined by the employer (on a basis approved by the Minister) to be in respect of employment in Canada.
@ref Reg 20(2) (src:287)
GIVEN `the employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the train is operated by a railway company within the meaning of the Canada Transportation Act whose principal place of business is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the employment determined by the employer to be in respect of employment in Canada` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister has approved the basis on which the employer determined it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 20(2) — the part of the employment on a train of a foreign railway company that is pensionable employment` `the employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train` `the train is operated by a railway company within the meaning of the Canada Transportation Act whose principal place of business is outside Canada` `the person is resident in Canada` `the part of the employment determined by the employer to be in respect of employment in Canada` `the Minister has approved the basis on which the employer determined it` MEANS
    IF     `the employment is in international transportation on a freight or passenger train`
       AND `the train is operated by a railway company within the meaning of the Canada Transportation Act whose principal place of business is outside Canada`
       AND `the person is resident in Canada`
       AND `the Minister has approved the basis on which the employer determined it`
    THEN JUST `the part of the employment determined by the employer to be in respect of employment in Canada`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 21: motor vehicles`

-- 21 Pensionable employment includes employment in international transportation on a motor vehicle that is
-- registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States, if (a)
-- the person so employed is resident in Canada; and (b) the motor vehicle is operated for the purposes of an
-- enterprise that is regarded, for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act, as an enterprise of Canada.
-- src:291 | 21 Pensionable employment includes employment in international transportation on a motor vehicle that is registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States, if
-- src:292 | (a) the person so employed is resident in Canada; and
-- src:293 | (b) the motor vehicle is operated for the purposes of an enterprise that is regarded, for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act, as an enterprise of Canada.
@ref Reg 21 (src:291-293)
GIVEN `the employment is in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person so employed is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motor vehicle is operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act as an enterprise of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 21 — pensionable employment includes the employment on the motor vehicle` `the employment is in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States` `the person so employed is resident in Canada` `the motor vehicle is operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act as an enterprise of Canada` MEANS
        `the employment is in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States`
    AND `the person so employed is resident in Canada`
    AND `the motor vehicle is operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act as an enterprise of Canada`
